%% ========================================================================
%% SECTION P — CROSS-FIELD CORRELATION: LOG(S1) vs ROTATION ANGLE
%%
%% PURPOSE
%% -------
%% Investigates the statistical relationship between two scalar fields
%% computed over the final map state:
%%
%% Field 1 — log(s1) : logarithmic stretch (largest singular value).
%% Field 2 — theta_R : rotation angle of the polar factor R = U*V'
%% (in radians, range [-pi, pi]).
%%
%% In a near-integrable system, low-stretch (KAM torus) regions typically
%% have near-zero rotation, while chaotic regions display a wider spread
%% of rotation angles. This section quantifies that relationship with:
%%
%% 1. A 2-D joint histogram of the two fields.
%% 2. A scatter plot coloured by spatial position.
%% 3. Pearson and Spearman correlation coefficients.
%% 4. Conditional mean: E[theta_R | log(s1)] — how average rotation
%% changes as stretch increases.
%%
%% FIGURES
%% -------
%% Fig 9010 : 2-D joint histogram of log(s1) vs theta_R (degrees).
%% Fig 9011 : Scatter plot coloured by row position (y coordinate).
%% Fig 9012 : Conditional mean theta_R vs binned log(s1).
